From: zrmnelson <104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:58:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] qml: give the command palette's search field a size

QtQuick.Templates.TextField has no implicit size, so the field collapsed to zero height: typing
still filtered the list, but the text and the focus border were invisible.
---
 modules/gui/qt/widgets/qml/ActionOverlay.qml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/gui/qt/widgets/qml/ActionOverlay.qml b/modules/gui/qt/widgets/qml/ActionOverlay.qml
index 4070cfbe5d..794c35bccc 100644
--- a/modules/gui/qt/widgets/qml/ActionOverlay.qml
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/widgets/qml/ActionOverlay.qml
@@ -190,6 +190,13 @@ FocusScope {
                 width: parent.width
                 focus: true
 
+                // The template control has no size of its own; without these it collapses to zero height
+                // and the typed text is invisible (filtering still works).
+                implicitWidth: parent.width
+                implicitHeight: Math.max(VLCStyle.dp(32, VLCStyle.scale),
+                                         contentHeight + topPadding + bottomPadding)
+                verticalAlignment: TextInput.AlignVCenter
+
                 placeholderText: root.isPalette ? qsTr("Type a command") : qsTr("Filter shortcuts")
                 color: theme.fg.primary
                 placeholderTextColor: theme.fg.secondary
